From 068b0ed0316252cd0f691f18f74e3e4834dbeafe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:15:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/51] Add the unsynced filter and lazy rendering, speed up
 backups, drop the Debug suffix

The word book's top bar gained an "Unsynced" checkbox: with it on,
the list shows only the words that have not reached Maimemo yet, and
the bar also carries a live count of them (tappable as a shortcut for
the filter). The list itself now renders lazily - one page of 60
cards at a time, the next page appended when the list nears its
rendered end - so a book of thousands of words binds only what is on
screen. Full-book operations (sync all, select all) still cover every
word, rendered or not.

Backups are written with maximum DEFLATE effort now: the database
and the subtitle cache are highly redundant, and the upload to
WebDAV/S3 is bounded by the archive size, so the extra compression
directly shortens the backup wait (measured against synthetic data:
the default level already compresses well, the top level trims a
little more at negligible CPU cost).

The debug launcher label is now plain "BiPipe" - the debug suffix
was a leftover of the NewPipe upstream convention.
